  "content": {
    "id": "p10-q28-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "28",
    "prompt": "Show that the sum of the squares of two consecutive triangular numbers is the triangular number of a perfect square.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": {
        "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
        "version": 1,
        "blocks": [
          {
            "id": "p10-q28-short-result",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "left",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "T_n^2+T_{n+1}^2=T_{(n+1)^2}",
                "display": false
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "p10-q28-short-method",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "left",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Substitute the triangular-number formula and factor to obtain a triangular number whose index is the perfect square ",
                "marks": []
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "(n+1)^2",
                "display": false
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ".",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "worked": "Using $T_n=\\dfrac{n(n+1)}{2}$,\n$$\\begin{align*}\nT_n^2+T_{n+1}^2&=\\left(\\frac{n(n+1)}{2}\\right)^2+\\left(\\frac{(n+1)(n+2)}{2}\\right)^2\\\\\nT_n^2+T_{n+1}^2&=\\frac14(n+1)^2\\left[n^2+(n+2)^2\\right]\\\\\nT_n^2+T_{n+1}^2&=\\frac14(n+1)^2(n^2+n^2+4n+4)\\\\\nT_n^2+T_{n+1}^2&=\\frac14(n+1)^2(2n^2+4n+4)\\\\\nT_n^2+T_{n+1}^2&=\\frac12(n+1)^2(n^2+2n+2)\\\\\nT_n^2+T_{n+1}^2&=\\frac12(n+1)^2\\left[(n+1)^2+1\\right]\\\\\nT_n^2+T_{n+1}^2&=T_{(n+1)^2}.\n\\end{align*}$$\nSince $(n+1)^2$ is a perfect square, the result follows.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 75
  },
